--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why GPL-2.0 and not something more permissive
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is not a preference. It is what the code's dependencies require.

  * bpf/skyline_cc.bpf.c reimplements algorithms from the Linux kernel
    closely enough that the kernel sources are cited by file and line
    throughout it, and in places reproduces their constants and control
    flow exactly. Those reimplementations exist because a cong_control
    struct_ops program bypasses the kernel's own versions and must supply
    an equivalent (see section 4 of docs/03-design.md). Work that close to
    GPL-2.0 originals is very likely derivative of them, and GPL-2.0
    section 6 forbids imposing further restrictions on recipients.

  * The three BPF objects declare `char LICENSE[] SEC("license") = "GPL"`.
    None of the helpers they currently call is GPL-only, so that
    declaration is not what makes them load today, but it is a statement
    to the kernel about their licensing and it needs to stay true.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream work referenced or reimplemented
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

No kernel source file is copied verbatim into this repository. Each
reference is cited inline at the point of use in bpf/skyline_cc.bpf.c.

  net/ipv4/tcp_cubic.c
      The cubic growth curve, the compute-K-once-per-epoch handling and the
      TCP-friendliness Reno floor, including the `delta = cwnd * 15 / 8`
      accumulator the kernel derives from beta_scale at its default beta,
      and the `cnt = 100 * cwnd` near-freeze when the target has not yet
      overtaken cwnd. Used by skyline_cubic_target() and the growth path
      that runs whenever the adaptive-cwnd module is off.
      TCP CUBIC: Copyright (C) 2007 Sangtae Ha, Injong Rhee
      and the Linux kernel contributors.

  net/ipv4/tcp_input.c
      Proportional Rate Reduction. A cong_control struct_ops program causes
      the kernel to skip its own PRR recovery-phase rate limiting entirely,
      so skyline_apply_prr() supplies an equivalent.
      Copyright (C) the Linux kernel contributors.

  net/ipv4/tcp_bbr.c
      Referenced for design, not reimplemented: BBR assigns cwnd from its
      own target each round rather than converging by additive increase,
      which is the approach skyline_set_cwnd_target() follows.
      TCP BBR: Copyright (C) 2016-2017 Google, Inc.

